# React Component Patterns

## Server vs client

```tsx
// ✅ Server component (default) — no directive, no hooks
export function StaticBlock() {
  return <section>...</section>;
}

// ✅ Client component — interactivity, hooks, Framer Motion
"use client";
export function AnimatedBlock() { ... }
```

Add `"use client"` only when the component uses hooks, browser APIs, or Framer Motion.

## Section structure

Follow existing sections (e.g. `contact.tsx`, `about.tsx`):

- Import `SectionHeading` for titles
- Use Framer Motion `motion.*` with `initial` / `whileInView` / `viewport={{ once: true }}`
- Keep section `id` attributes stable for navbar links

## Animations

```tsx
const fadeUp = {
  initial: { opacity: 0, y: 24 },
  animate: { opacity: 1, y: 0 },
};
```

Prefer subtle motion. Use `useSpring` / `useTransform` sparingly (see `hero.tsx`).

## Images

Use `next/image` with explicit `width`, `height`, and meaningful `alt` text.

## Forms

- Client-side: controlled state or react-hook-form
- Submit to `/api/contact` via `fetch`
- Show feedback with `sonner` toasts (`toast.success`, `toast.error`)
